---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

const blogSchema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "Article",
  "headline": "Aerosol Propellants Explained: LPG vs DME vs HFC vs N₂ vs CO₂",
  "author": {
    "@type": "Person",
    "name": "Absar Khan"
  },
  "publisher": {
    "@type": "Organization",
    "name": "Global Aerosols",
    "logo": {
      "@type": "ImageObject",
      "url": "https://www.globalaerosols.com/logo.png"
    }
  },
  "mainEntityOfPage": {
    "@type": "WebPage",
    "@id": "https://www.globalaerosols.com/aerosol-propellants-explained-lpg-vs-dme-vs-hfc-vs-n2-vs-co2"
  },
  "datePublished": "2025-11-12",
  "dateModified": "2025-11-12"
};
const breadcrumbSchema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
  "itemListElement": [
    {
      "@type": "ListItem",
      "position": 1,
      "name": "Aerosol Propellants",
      "item": "https://www.globalaerosols.com/aerosol-propellants-explained-lpg-vs-dme-vs-hfc-vs-n2-vs-co2"
    }
  ]
};
const schemas = [blogSchema, breadcrumbSchema];
---

<Layout
  title="Aerosol Propellants Explained: LPG vs DME vs HFC vs N₂ vs CO₂ for Indian & Global Manufacturers | Global Aerosols"
  description="Technical guide to aerosol propellants including LPG, DME, HFC, nitrogen, carbon dioxide and compressed air for Indian and global manufacturers."
  canonical="https://www.globalaerosols.com/aerosol-propellants-explained-lpg-vs-dme-vs-hfc-vs-n2-vs-co2"
  ogImage="https://assets.zyrosite.com/A3QlOV94WLSaL6xE/aerosol-can-cross-section-components.jpg-rgcWcHa1iiQgJsa9.png"
  ogType="article"
  schemaJson={schemas}
>
  <main class="section-container" style="max-width: 100%; padding-left: 48px; padding-right: 48px; padding-top: 40px; padding-bottom: 80px;">
    
    <!-- HTML5 Compliant Breadcrumbs -->
    <nav aria-label="Breadcrumb" style="display: flex; gap: 8px; font-size: 0.85rem; color: var(--text-muted); margin-bottom: 24px; font-family: 'Inter', sans-serif;">
      <a href="/" style="color: var(--text-muted);">Home</a>
      <span>&gt;</span>
      <a href="/blog" style="color: var(--text-muted);">Blog</a>
      <span>&gt;</span>
      <span style="color: var(--text-primary); font-weight: 500;">Aerosols & Gas Dosing</span>
    </nav>

    <!-- Main article container -->
    <article class="blog-prose">
      <header class="post-header">
        <h1 class="gradient-text" style="font-size: 3rem; line-height: 1.15; font-weight: 900; margin-bottom: 20px;">
          Aerosol Propellants Explained: LPG vs DME vs HFC vs N₂ vs CO₂ for Indian & Global Manufacturers
        </h1>
        
        <!-- Post meta details -->
        <div style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 16px; font-size: 0.9rem; color: var(--text-muted); margin-bottom: 30px; font-family: 'Inter', sans-serif; font-weight: 500; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); padding-bottom: 20px;">
          <div style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 8px;">
            <span style="width: 28px; height: 28px; background: var(--primary); color: white; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; border-radius: 50%; font-weight: 700; font-size: 0.75rem;">AK</span>
            <span>By <strong>Absar Khan</strong></span>
          </div>
          <span style="width: 4px; height: 4px; border-radius: 50%; background-color: var(--border);"></span>
          <span>Published: <strong>Nov 12, 2025</strong></span>
          <span style="width: 4px; height: 4px; border-radius: 50%; background-color: var(--border);"></span>
          <span>Reading Time: <strong>18 min read</strong></span>
          <span style="width: 4px; height: 4px; border-radius: 50%; background-color: var(--border);"></span>
          <span style="background: #e0f2fe; color: #0369a1; padding: 2px 10px; border-radius: 50px; font-size: 0.75rem; font-weight: 700; text-transform: uppercase;">Aerosols & Gas Dosing</span>
        </div>
      </header>

      <!-- Primary Featured Image -->
      <div class="image-slot">
        <img 
          src="https://assets.zyrosite.com/A3QlOV94WLSaL6xE/aerosol-can-cross-section-components.jpg-rgcWcHa1iiQgJsa9.png" 
          alt="Cross section of aerosol can showing liquid propellant vapor phase dip tube and valve" 
          width="1200" 
          height="800" 
          loading="eager" 
        />
      </div>

      <!-- Table of Contents -->
      <div class="box" style="background: #f8fafc; border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: var(--radius-lg); padding: 24px; margin: 30px 0;">
        <h3 style="margin-top: 0; font-family: 'Outfit', sans-serif; color: var(--text-primary); font-size: 1.25rem; font-weight: 700; border-bottom: 2px solid var(--border); padding-bottom: 8px;">Guide Contents</h3>
        <ul style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(280px, 1fr)); gap: 10px; list-style-type: none; padding-left: 0; margin-bottom: 0;">
          
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="lead">
      

      <div class="toc-box">
  <strong>Table of Contents</strong>
  <ol style="margin:8px 0 0 18px;padding:0;">
    <li>What Is a Propellant in an Aerosol System?</li>
    <li>Why Propellant Selection Is Critical for Product Success</li>
    <li>Types of Aerosol Propellants – Technical Overview
      <ol style="margin-top:6px;">
        <li>LPG (Liquefied Petroleum Gas)</li>
        <li>DME (Dimethyl Ether)</li>
        <li>HFCs (Hydrofluorocarbons)</li>
        <li>Nitrogen (N₂)</li>
        <li>Carbon Dioxide (CO₂)</li>
        <li>Compressed Air</li>
      </ol>
    </li>
    <li>Technical Comparison of All Major Propellants</li>
    <li>Cost Comparison of Aerosol Propellants (India vs Global)</li>
    <li>Environmental &amp; Regulatory Perspective</li>
    <li>How to Select the Right Propellant for Your Product</li>
    <li>Common Formulation Problems Linked to Wrong Propellant Selection</li>
    <li>Future of Aerosol Propellants – Trends &amp; Innovations</li>
    <li>How Global Aerosols Supports Propellant Selection &amp; Compliance</li>
    <li>Frequently Asked Questions (FAQ)</li>
    <li>For Deeper Understanding of the Aerosol Ecosystem</li>
    <li>Selected External Technical References</li>
    <li>Get Expert Aerosol Guidance</li>
    <li>About the Author</li>
  </ol>
<div class="cta-box"></div>



      <!-- Contact Box -->
      <div class="cta" style="background: linear-gradient(135deg, var(--primary) 0%, var(--secondary) 100%); color: #ffffff; padding: 30px; border-radius: var(--radius-lg); margin-top: 40px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start; gap: 20px; md-flex-direction: row; md-align-items: center;">
        <div class="left">
          <p style="margin:0 0 8px 0; font-size:1.25rem; font-weight:800; font-family: 'Outfit', sans-serif;">Need Technical Support for Aerosol Formulations?</p>
          <p style="margin:0 0 16px 0; font-size:0.95rem; line-height:1.6; opacity:0.95;">
            Partner with Global Aerosols to audit, scale up, and troubleshoot your aerosol chemistry, canister pressure calculations, filling lines, and safety systems.
          </p>
          <p style="margin:0; font-size:0.9rem; line-height:1.6; font-family: monospace;">
            Email: <strong>consulting@globalaerosols.com</strong><br />
            Website: <a href="/" style="color: #ffffff; font-weight: 600; text-decoration: underline;">https://www.globalaerosols.com</a><br />
            Phone: <strong>+91 9819548320 &nbsp;&nbsp; +91 8169102990</strong>
          </p>
        </div>
        <a href="mailto:consulting@globalaerosols.com" class="btn" style="background:#ffffff; color:var(--primary); font-weight:700; padding:12px 24px; border-radius:var(--radius-sm); border:none; text-decoration:none; transition: all var(--transition-fast);">
          Request Consultation
        </a>
      </div>

      <!-- ABOUT THE AUTHOR -->
      <section class="section" id="about-author" style="margin-top: 50px; background: #f8fafc; border: 1px solid var(--border); padding: 30px; border-radius: var(--radius-lg); display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 20px; md-flex-direction: row;">
        <div style="flex-shrink: 0; width: 60px; height: 60px; background: linear-gradient(135deg, var(--primary) 0%, var(--secondary) 100%); color: white; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; border-radius: 50%; font-size: 1.5rem; font-weight: 800; font-family: 'Outfit', sans-serif; box-shadow: var(--shadow-md);">
          AK
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3 style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 8px; font-family: 'Outfit', sans-serif; font-size: 1.3rem; font-weight: 700; color: var(--text-primary);">About the Specialist</h3>
          <p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 12px; font-size: 0.95rem; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--text-muted);">
            <strong>Absar Khan</strong> is the principal consultant and chemical formulation architect at <strong>Global Formulation</strong>. He possesses cross-disciplinary engineering expertise spanning aerosol gassing systems, pharmaceutical manufacturing, sterile injectables, cosmetics, and green chemical plant setups. Absar leads scientific and engineering advisory teams supporting manufacturers globally in technology selection, GMP layouts, validation frameworks, and regulatory strategies.
          </p>
          <p style="margin: 0; font-size: 0.9rem;">
            <strong>LinkedIn Portfolio:</strong> 
            <a 
              href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/absar-khan-aerosol-consultant-and-formulator-78359b162" 
              style="font-weight: 700; color: var(--primary); text-decoration: underline;"
            >
              Connect with Absar Khan on LinkedIn
            </a>
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Footer copyright -->
      <footer style="text-align: center; margin-top: 50px; color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 0.85rem; font-family: 'Inter', sans-serif;">
        &copy; {new Date().getFullYear()} Global Aerosols. All rights reserved. 
        <br />
        <span style="font-size: 0.75rem; opacity: 0.8;">Centralised Aerosol Dosing &amp; Chemical Scale-Up Engineering.</span>
      </footer>

    </article>
  </main>
</Layout>

<style>
  .blog-prose h1, 
  .blog-prose h2, 
  .blog-prose h3 {
    font-family: 'Playfair Display', 'Outfit', serif !important;
  }

  .blog-prose p, 
  .blog-prose ul, 
  .blog-prose ol,
  .blog-prose h3,
  .blog-prose .lead,
  .blog-prose .box,
  .blog-prose .cta,
  .blog-prose .table-container,
  .blog-prose #faq {
    max-width: 100%;
    width: 100%;
  }

  .blog-prose .lead {
    margin: 2rem 0;
  }
</style>
